enter/leave, C = recursive arc (cut edge). diag2.sh (vc dir holding c2y.dll + run.sh) -> build/ord.txt.
Link output == normal link except PE timestamp.
dfs.py ord.txt roots|cuts|path NAME|kids NAME ; cuts.py ord.txt [name] (F/X based).
Dec.java: Ghidra headless decompile of fns containing given addrs.
c2 order (PINNED, decompiled): 1070c919 -> DFS 1070ce78 over node list 1087f4c8 (roots = reverse obj
link order, reverse fn order; edges = callee first-declaration order in the TU); edge to an on-stack node
gets flag 1 (cut, "is a recursive arc"); 1070cfdf then emits fns by repeated leaf-peel passes over the
sym list 10881d68 ignoring cut edges. Cuts alone decide callee-before-caller.

